'''Jail Break Tunnel''' (脱獄トンネル, ''Datsugoku Tonneru'', '''Jailbreak Tunnel''') is the 18th sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 2.3 Update#Version 2.3.1 Update|Version 2.3.1]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], it is the 11th sub-chapter in the Stories of Legend and is available up to 3★ difficulty.

==Difficulty==
For most, Jail Break Tunnel is the hardest sub-chapter up to this point. Except for [[Prison Sentence]], every stage has potential to be quite challenging, with [[Sin and Punishment]] and [[Harry Tunnel]] being arguably the toughest on higher difficulties. You will also need a ranged [[Critical Hit|Critter]] like [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] for [[Dead Falls]], which introduces [[Sir Metal Seal]]. Dont take the other stages lightly, though, as [[Pitfall Zone]] is actually a very underestimated timed stage.
{{LegendDiff|150|170|150}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces two new enemies:
*[[Sir Metal Seal]]: A powerful [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[Sir Seal]] with high attack power, decent range for a Metal enemy, and very high health compared to previous Metals.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Enemy)|Ururun Wolf]]: A boss enemy that appears in [[The Great Escaper|the final stage]]. Has very high HP and long range, but gets knocked back a lot and has somewhat weak attacks.
This sub-chapter starts the trend of having unlockable bosses as [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] in a Stories of Legend sub-chapter - the final stage has a 30% chance to drop [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] (guaranteed if a [[Treasure Radar]] is used) whereas the Nintendo Switch port is guaranteed.

